// Package wl is the Wayland client: the runtime over libwayland-client, which
// is bound with purego, and the Go bindings of every protocol in
// ../protocols, generated by `glutter-gen wayland` into the *_gen.go files.
//
// The generated code gives each interface a Go type (WlSurface), typed request
// methods (Attach), a struct of typed event callbacks (WlSurfaceEvents) and
// the enum constants. The runtime owns the things the generated code stands
// on: the C struct mirrors, the interface tables in C memory, the single event
// dispatcher shared by all proxies, and the connection.
//
// Like the libraries it wraps, a Conn and its objects belong to the UI thread
// (docs/SPEC.md §8.1 rule 4).
//
// Flutter: no counterpart.
package wl

//go:generate go run ../../../../../cmd/glutter-gen wayland -protocols ../protocols -out .
